// Title: Disk Image Creation Via Hdiutil - MacOS
// Sigma ID: 1cf98dc2-fcb0-47c9-8aea-654c9284d1ae
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Omar Khaled (@beacon_exe)
// Date: 2024-08-10 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: exfiltration
// Description: Detects the execution of the hdiutil utility in order to create a disk image.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate usage of hdiutil by administrators and users.
// References:
//   - https://www.loobins.io/binaries/hdiutil/
//   - https://www.sentinelone.com/blog/from-the-front-linesunsigned-macos-orat-malware-gambles-for-the-win/
//   - https://ss64.com/mac/hdiutil.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_hdiutil_create.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/hdiutil" and ProcessCommandLine contains "create"
